OK, the VAX 8550 upgrade was a jumper on the backplane to get the speed
increase. The 8500 was too fast when it was finished so the microcode was
filled up with NOP's and a jumper put in place to make them run. when you
got an 8550 upgrade for $20,000, you got a new backplane with the jumper in
place and new microcode load. Customers figured they were getting something
special with a new backplane exchange. The 8530 figures in here somewhere
too.

rtt




