> same in this regard.  As I understand it, the a series is supposed to
> be more geared towards IDE drives than the au's.

The 600a and 600au are the same basic systems. The differences
are the graphics card and the SCSI-Controller (and the console).

There are two models of the PWS itself (MiataMX5 and MiataGL).
If you have a PWS with USB your 600a is the newer MiataGL model
which has another IDE chipset as the MiataMX5.

MiataMX5 - Intel IDE Chip
MiataGL - Cypress IDE Chip

For OpenVMS you need the Cypress IDE Chipset or a SCSI CD-ROM
to install OpenVMS via CD.

